vendor-probe-autocad-bricscad-divergences — real AutoCAD-vs-BricsCAD differences surfaced by the vendor probes
=============================================================================================================

Source: vendor:probes:autocad job 15538718100 (AutoCAD 2022, alfe 1.6.13,
Windows runner). With the no-&rest princ-capture fix (1.6.13) the AutoCAD probe
output is finally readable, and it now produces real verdicts. BricsCAD (macOS
+ Windows) is 100% green on the same probes; AutoCAD fails 14 assertions. These
are GENUINE BricsCAD-vs-AutoCAD divergences -- the whole point of the vendor
tail. clautolisp currently tracks BricsCAD's (more lenient) behaviour.

PROCESS (pjb) for EACH divergence below:
  1. Document it in autolisp-spec (per-vendor, in the *** vendor/clautolisp
     section of the affected function page + the user manual).
  2. Implement it per --dialect in clautolisp:
       --dialect autocad    -> AutoCAD's behaviour
       --dialect bricscad    -> BricsCAD's behaviour
       --dialect clautolisp -> a deliberate choice/extension (often the lenient
                               superset, possibly WARN)
       --dialect strict      -> the conservative/portable option (usually the
                               STRICTER of the two, so code that passes strict
                               runs on both vendors)
  3. Fork an issue to update cadaptor, which also tracks bricscad/autocad
     differences.
Each numbered divergence can be forked into its own spec+dialect+cadaptor issue.

DIAGNOSTIC GAP: the probes only print ok/FAIL, not the divergent VALUE. To spec
these accurately we need to SEE what AutoCAD actually returns (regapp -> nil or
T? entmakex on a marker-less ELLIPSE -> nil?). Add a diagnostic probe variant
(or a --verbose mode) that prints the actual return on a mismatch, and re-run on
AutoCAD, before finalising the spec wording.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Divergence 1 — entmake/entmakex requires subclass markers for R13+ entities
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence (entity-lifecycle, 4 fails): entmakex returns nil (no ENAME) on AutoCAD
for ELLIPSE, LWPOLYLINE, RAY, XLINE; passes for LINE, POINT, CIRCLE, ARC, TEXT,
SOLID, 3DFACE. The probe's entmakex data for the failing four omits the
subclass-marker records, e.g.:
    (list (cons 0 "ELLIPSE") (cons 10 ...) (cons 11 ...) (cons 40 ..) ...)
i.e. no (100 . "AcDbEntity") / (100 . "AcDbEllipse").

Analysis: real AutoCAD's entmake/entmakex requires the group-100 subclass
markers for post-R12 entities (ELLIPSE, LWPOLYLINE, RAY, XLINE, MTEXT, LEADER,
SPLINE, HATCH, …); the R12-era entities (LINE/POINT/CIRCLE/ARC/TEXT/SOLID/
3DFACE/…) accept data without them. BricsCAD is lenient -- it synthesises the
markers -- and clautolisp follows BricsCAD.

Actions:
  * spec: document entmake's subclass-marker requirement; table of which entity
    types need (100 . "AcDbEntity")+(100 . "AcDb<Type>"). Note AutoCAD=required,
    BricsCAD=optional.
  * dialect: autocad -> reject (return nil) marker-less R13+ data; bricscad ->
    accept, synthesise markers; clautolisp -> accept (lenient), consider WARN;
    strict -> require markers (the portable choice, matches AutoCAD).
  * cadaptor fork.
Confidence: HIGH (well-documented AutoLISP behaviour).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Divergence 2 — regapp / XData round-trip (cascades to ssget "X" selection)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence:
  * drawing-data: "regapp of a fresh app returns the name" FAILS
    -- the probe checks (= (regapp app) app).
  * selection: ALL EIGHT (mine)-XData-filtered ssget "X" tests fail
    (-3 app, type=LINE, type=LINE,CIRCLE, OR/AND/NOT colour, colour>1, and
    sslength=3). BUT "ssget X (-3 OTHERAPP) selects none" PASSES.
    (mine) = (-3 (app...)) XData filter over the seeded entities.

Analysis: ssget "X" itself works on AutoCAD (the OTHERAPP=0 case passed). The
seeded entities carry private XData under *app*, and the (mine) filter finds
NONE of them -> the regapp+XData-attach path diverges: either regapp returns a
different value (name vs nil vs T) and/or the XData set via entmod doesn't stick
/ isn't visible to the ssget -3 filter on AutoCAD as it is on BricsCAD.

Needs vendor confirmation of the exact difference (see DIAGNOSTIC GAP): print
(regapp app), and after seeding print (entget e '("*")) to see whether the -3
XData is actually attached on AutoCAD.

Actions: spec + dialect + cadaptor (same structure) once the exact behaviour is
captured. Likely two sub-divergences: (2a) regapp return value; (2b) XData
attach/visibility under ssget -3.
Confidence: MEDIUM (cascade root identified; exact vendor behaviour to confirm).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Divergence 3 — entmod on an XRECORD readback
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence (drawing-data, 1 fail): "entmod on the xrecord reads back the new
value" fails. The probe entmakex's an XRECORD (with the (100 . "AcDbXrecord")
marker, so creation succeeds), then entmod-mutates it and reads it back; the
readback diverges on AutoCAD.

Analysis: entmod on a non-graphical dictionary object (XRECORD) may be
restricted or behave differently on AutoCAD vs BricsCAD (AutoCAD may require
the change via the dictionary / a different code path, or reject entmod on
xrecords). Confirm the actual readback.

Actions: spec + dialect + cadaptor. Confidence: MEDIUM.

