Related
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The scenario dir already carries per-vendor expected captures
(entity-lifecycle-{autocad,bricscad}.sexp, etc.). Once each divergence's true
AutoCAD behaviour is confirmed, update the AutoCAD .sexp expectations to match,
so the conformance harness encodes the vendor difference rather than reporting
a raw FAIL. The vendor probes' single "ALL … PASSED" gate is fine for BricsCAD
(green) but for AutoCAD should become per-vendor-aware (expect the documented
divergences) OR the divergences get fixed in clautolisp's autocad dialect and
the probe data made portable (add the markers).

MEASURED values (job 15538912809, probes with failure-DIAG)
-----------------------------------------------------------
Diagnostics landed; the re-run gives the exact AutoCAD returns:

  D1 entmakex ELLIPSE/LWPOLYLINE/RAY/XLINE  -> type=nil val=nil  (rejected, not
     an error) -- CONFIRMED. AutoCAD requires (100 . "AcDb...") markers.
  D2 (regapp "CLAUTOLISP_DDP")              -> nil  (BricsCAD: the name).
     CONFIRMED. Registration still WORKS (selection DIAG shows the XData
     attaches), only the RETURN VALUE differs -- AutoCAD returns nil.
  D3 entmod on an XRECORD                   -> readback group1 = "payload"
     (the OLD value), want "payload2". CONFIRMED & sharper than thought:
     entmod on an xrecord is a NO-OP on AutoCAD (the mutation doesn't take);
     BricsCAD updates it. (Real AutoCAD wants xrecord edits via the object /
     vlax-put, not entmod.)
  Selection -> NOT a language divergence: DIAG shows the -3 XData attaches
     (YES) and ssget "X" filters, but mine-filter=8 (want 4) and ssget X
     all=36. Each probe opens a FRESH temp copy of empty.dwg, so the runner's
     c:/gitlab-runner/dwg/empty.dwg is CONTAMINATED -- ~32 stray entities, 4 of
     them already carrying the probe's private app XData (an ancient probe
     ._QSAVE, from before the temp-copy hygiene). => drawing-hygiene, not a
     divergence. BricsCAD passes (=4) because its empty.dwg copy is clean AND it
     uses _QUIT _N (no save).

Confirmed divergences to process (spec + dialect + cadaptor each):
  D1 entmake subclass markers for R13+ entities   (autocad reject / bricscad
     synthesise / clautolisp lenient+WARN / strict require).
  D2 regapp return value: autocad nil, bricscad the name  (registration
     identical; only the return differs).
  D3 entmod on non-graphical XRECORD: autocad no-op, bricscad updates.

Actions before Divergence 2/3 spec text is final: none -- the values are now
measured. Selection: regenerate a truly-empty c:/gitlab-runner/dwg/empty.dwg on
the runner (and consider making the AutoCAD probe save-free like BricsCAD:
run.scr `._QSAVE`/`._QUIT _Y` -> `._QUIT _N`, tested carefully for the
accoreconsole prompt) then re-run to confirm selection is green / surfaces any
real ssget "X" divergence underneath.

